/addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OISHI, KENGO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SOHDA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA MORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OISHI KENGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SOHDA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, MORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OISHI, KENGO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SOHDA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A magnetic disk cartridge (1) for enhancing the function of preventing a shutter member from coming off because of case deformation due to the shock or bend when the cartridge drops. A disk-shaped magnetic disk medium (6) is rotatably housed in a case (C) which is defined by an upper shell (2) and a lower shell (3). On the end portion of an engaging portion (46) engaging with one end portion of an elastic member (7) of a connecting plate portion (42) of a shutter member (4) for opening/closing a magnetic head loading opening (11) of the case (C), a restraining protrusion (47) is provided which protrudes into a slitlike opening (19) through which the engaging portion (46) slides, so as to restrain deformation of the upper shell (2) and the lower shell (3) in the direction where the slitlike opening (19) is narrowed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une cartouche (1) de disque magnétique présentant une amélioration de la fonction, selon laquelle un volet ne peut se détacher du carter suite à sa déformation due à un choc ou à une flexion lorsque ladite cartouche tombe. Un support (6) de disque magnétique en forme de disque est logé rotatif dans le carter (C) défini par une partie de boîtier supérieure (2) et une partie de boîtier inférieure (3). Sur la partie d'extrémité d'une partie de contact (46) venant en contact avec une partie extrémité d'un élément élastique (7) d'une partie plaque de connexion (42) d'un volet (4), qui permet l'ouverture/fermeture d'une ouverture de chargement (11) de tête magnétique du carter (C), une saillie de retenue (47) dépasse dans une ouverture de type fente (19) à travers laquelle la partie de contact (46) coulisse, de manière à réduire la déformation de la partie de boîtier supérieur (2) et de la partie de boîtier inférieur (3) dans le sens où l'ouverture de type fente (19) est rétrécie.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>